# Contributing Guidelines

Standards for contributing code to Studio Tech Engineering projects.

Apply when: creating branches, writing commits, submitting merge requests, or reviewing code.

---

## Rule Strength Tags

| Tag     | Meaning                                                          |
|---------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| [HARD]  | Must not be broken. Refuse conflicting requests.                 |
| [WARN]  | Default behavior. Explain trade-off if user wants to deviate.    |
| [GUIDE] | Recommendation. Follow unless user has clear reason to deviate.  |

---

## Precedence

[HARD] Repository-specific files (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`) take precedence over this blueprint.

---

## Development Workflow

1. **Create branch** from `main`: `{branch_type}-{ISSUE}-{description}`
2. **Make changes** with atomic commits using Conventional Commits
3. **Rebase** on `origin/main` before pushing
4. **Create MR** with clear title, description, and `Closes #ISSUE`
5. **Code review** — respond to feedback, keep branch current
6. **Merge** after CI passes and approval received
7. **Delete branch** after merge

---

## Branch Strategy

| Branch  | Purpose                                                   |
|---------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| `main`  | [HARD] Production-ready code                              |
| Feature | [HARD] Format: `{branch_type}-{ISSUE}-{description}`      |

[HARD] Valid branch types: `feature`, `bugfix`, `hotfix`

Example: `feature-123-add-auth`, `bugfix-456-fix-login`

---

## Commit Guidelines

| Rule                                      | Example                                              |
|-------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| [HARD] Conventional Commits format        | `feat: add user auth`, `fix: resolve bug`            |
| [HARD] Valid types only                   | feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore |
| [HARD] Imperative mood                    | `add feature` not `added feature`                    |
| [HARD] Lowercase after prefix             | `feat: add` not `feat: Add`                          |
| [HARD] Subject under 72 characters        | Keep subject line concise                            |
| [HARD] No AI attribution                  | Never add "Co-authored-by: AI" or similar            |
| [WARN] Single-line preferred              | Body only when essential for complex changes         |
| [GUIDE] Atomic commits                    | One logical change per commit                        |

---

## Merge Request Process

[HARD] Before creating MR:

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
git push --force-with-lease origin <branch>
```

**MR requirements:**

| Requirement                            | Details                                             |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| [HARD] Rebased on main                 | No merge conflicts, clean history                   |
| [HARD] Clear title                     | Under 72 characters, descriptive                    |
| [HARD] Description                     | What changed, why, testing performed                |
| [HARD] Links issue                     | Include `Closes #ISSUE` in description              |
| [HARD] No AI attribution               | Never mention AI assistance in title or description |
| [HARD] CI checks passing               | All pipelines green                                 |
| [HARD] Code review approval            | At least one team member                            |
| [GUIDE] Tests added                    | Coverage thresholds met                             |
| [GUIDE] Docs updated                   | If APIs or behavior changed                         |

---

## Code Review

| Role     | Responsibilities                                                            |
|----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Author   | Keep MRs focused, provide context, respond to feedback, keep branch current |
| Reviewer | Verify tests, check CI passes, consider architecture, look for security issues |

---

## Quick Reference

| Task          | Pattern                                                              |
|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Create branch | `{branch_type}-{ISSUE}-{description}`                                |
| Write commit  | `type: description` (imperative, lowercase, <72 chars)               |
| Before MR     | Rebase on `origin/main`, push with `--force-with-lease`              |
| Commit types  | feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore       |

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Branch named with type and issue number
- [ ] Commits use Conventional Commits format
- [ ] Subject line under 72 characters
- [ ] No AI attribution in commits or MR
- [ ] Branch rebased on `origin/main` before MR
- [ ] MR has clear title and `Closes #ISSUE`
- [ ] CI checks passing
- [ ] No secrets committed